<attribute name="presentationName" nodeId="97337d1a">Develop training delivery schedule</attribute>
<attribute name="briefDescription" nodeId="a7c95b12"></attribute>
<attribute name="suppressed" nodeId="8cbb9171">false</attribute>
<attribute name="orderingGuide" nodeId="4ad41f3"></attribute>
<attribute name="authors" nodeId="2f7fc14f"></attribute>
<attribute name="changeDate" nodeId="ca0dd8a1">Wed Feb 22 10:44:07 EST 2017</attribute>
<attribute name="changeDescription" nodeId="d9444126">FEB 2017 - removed optional inputs Organizational Change Plan, Communications Plan</attribute>
<attribute name="version" nodeId="a2da0c27"></attribute>
<attribute name="mainDescription" nodeId="13cd6a4a">&lt;p&gt;
    Ensure training logistics sync with project milestones and take into account when skills are needed during
    implementation.&amp;nbsp; Decreasing the gap between knowledge acquistion and knowledge usage (on the job)&amp;nbsp; correlates
    with increases in training effectiveness.&amp;nbsp; Part of the process of developing the schedule includes finalizing
    trainers, communicating training sessions and updating collateral around learner needs (as curriculum development often
    uncovers new learner needs).
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Develop initial training schedule for all courses and locations that captures how how training will be rolled out
        such as by end user, role, team, or location.
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Work with the key stakeholders to understand any constraints around the schedule such as non-working days, shift
        patterns, or black out periods.
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Share the initial training schedule with other program team to test and highlight dependencies, agree with key
        stakeholders, and engage any active business readiness networks
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</attribute>
<attribute name="externalId" nodeId="9f0e3a60"></attribute>
<attribute name="keyConsiderations" nodeId="db45f656"></attribute>
<attribute name="longPresentationName" nodeId="41350d72"></attribute>
<attribute name="purpose" nodeId="a8ec70d4">&lt;p&gt;
    To ensure that training is delivered within acceptable tolerances for duration, cost, and quality; to proactively plan
    training resources against learner availability.
&lt;/p&gt;</attribute>
